<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela union to strike if oil prices raised.</title>
<headline>Venezuela union to strike if oil prices raised.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuela's largest union, the Confederation of Venezuelan Workers (CTV), said Wednesday it would launch a national strike if domestic gasoline prices were raised, CTV secretary general Carlos Navarro said.</p>
<p>&quot;Given the way things are, the circumstances of the country and the extreme economic pressures that workers face, there should not be a gasoline price increase,&quot; Navarro said in a Radio Caracas interview.</p>
<p>But Planning Minister Teodoro Petkoff, in a separate radio interview, said gasoline prices had to be raised some time this year.  The long expected price hike forms part of a letter of agreement signed with the International Monetary Fund last year.</p>
<p>((-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
